0
00:00:07,445 --> 00:00:09,448
PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"...

1
00:00:09,448 --> 00:00:12,617
ON THE WAY TO LONDON, KIM WAS
CONFRONTED ABOUT TALKING

2
00:00:12,617 --> 00:00:14,119
BEHIND PEOPLE'S BACKS...

3
00:00:14,119 --> 00:00:16,588
YOU HAVE TALKED ABOUT
EVERYBODY IN THIS HOUSE,

4
00:00:16,588 --> 00:00:18,290
AND THIS IS NOT VENTING.

5
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:20,392
THIS IS YOU BEING OBNOXIOUS.

6
00:00:20,392 --> 00:00:21,493
LIKE I'M SORRY.

7
00:00:21,493 --> 00:00:25,030
AND LIKE SOMETIMES
I JUST DON'T KNOW.

8
00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:28,100
BUT THE CONFRONTATIONS KEPT
COMING WHEN THE GIRLS HAD

9
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,136
THEIR FIRST ENCOUNTER
WITH THE PAPARAZZI...

10
00:00:31,136 --> 00:00:32,170
NO, SORRY.

11
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,139
OKAY, GUYS, GET YOUR PICTURE.

12
00:00:34,139 --> 00:00:35,807
AND DESPITE
A FIERCE PHOTO SHOOT,

13
00:00:35,807 --> 00:00:37,342
LISA TURNED SOME JUDGES OFF...

14
00:00:37,342 --> 00:00:40,278
DON'T YOU THINK SOMETIMES
LISA IS TOO IN YOUR FACE,

15
00:00:40,278 --> 00:00:41,646
TOO MISS PERSONALITY?

16
00:00:41,646 --> 00:00:43,281
...AND SHE WAS SENT HOME.

17
00:00:43,281 --> 00:00:44,750
JAYLA.

18
00:00:47,352 --> 00:00:48,453
FIVE GIRLS REMAIN.

19
00:00:48,453 --> 00:00:51,056
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

20
00:00:52,224 --> 00:00:56,261
♪♪♪

21
00:01:41,106 --> 00:01:43,008
IT WAS A VERY,
VERY SURPRISING

22
00:01:43,008 --> 00:01:45,076
AND SHOCKING ELIMINATION.

23
00:01:45,076 --> 00:01:47,045
WILL LISA AND JAYLA
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

24
00:01:47,045 --> 00:01:49,247
LISA WAS SOMEONE
THAT I THOUGHT

25
00:01:49,247 --> 00:01:51,116
WOULD BE IN THE TOP THREE
FOR THE WHOLE TIME

26
00:01:51,116 --> 00:01:52,350
I'VE BEEN HERE.

27
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:53,685
JAYLA.

28
00:01:53,685 --> 00:01:55,353
WHEN THEY CALLED
JAYLA'S NAME,

29
00:01:55,353 --> 00:01:58,423
OUR MOUTHS DROPPED LIKE, "WHAT?"

30
00:01:58,423 --> 00:02:00,992
IT'S OKAY. BYE-BYE.

31
00:02:00,992 --> 00:02:02,994
IT'S SCARY JUST TO KNOW
THAT SHE CAN DO SO GOOD

32
00:02:02,994 --> 00:02:04,996
AND SHE CAN GO HOME,
WHICH MEANS, YOU KNOW,

33
00:02:04,996 --> 00:02:08,200
ANY OF US CAN GO HOME
LIKE THAT.

34
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,601
HOW AMAZING WOULD THAT BE
IF YOU AND I WERE IN

35
00:02:09,601 --> 00:02:10,502
THE TOP THREE TOGETHER?

36
00:02:10,502 --> 00:02:11,970
AAH!

37
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:13,572
LIKE IF YOU WON,
I'D BE SO HAPPY, DUDE.

38
00:02:13,572 --> 00:02:15,040
SERIOUSLY. NO, SERIOUSLY.

39
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,541
WHAT HAPPENED IN THE LIMO
WAS COMPLETELY BLOWN

40
00:02:16,541 --> 00:02:18,043
OUT OF PROPORTION.

41
00:02:18,043 --> 00:02:20,412
YOU HAVE TALKED ABOUT
EVERYBODY IN THIS HOUSE,

42
00:02:20,412 --> 00:02:22,380
AND THIS IS NOT VENTING.

43
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:24,983
THIS IS YOU BEING OBNOXIOUS.

44
00:02:24,983 --> 00:02:27,018
WE'VE PUT OUR PROBLEMS ASIDE,
WE'VE DEALT WITH THEM.

45
00:02:27,018 --> 00:02:28,954
AND WE ALSO
CARE ABOUT EACH OTHER

46
00:02:28,954 --> 00:02:30,155
AND WANT TO HELP EACH OTHER OUT.

47
00:02:30,155 --> 00:02:31,990
WE STARTED...

48
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:33,391
WAY DOWN...

49
00:02:33,391 --> 00:02:34,559
WELL, YOU STARTED
A LITTLE HIGHER THAN ME.

50
00:02:34,559 --> 00:02:35,961
BUT WE STARTED PRETTY LOW.

51
00:02:35,961 --> 00:02:37,996
BEING IN LONDON MAKES THINGS
MORE INTENSE.

52
00:02:37,996 --> 00:02:40,732
THE COMPETITION GETS STIFFER,
THE PICTURES ARE ALL BEAUTIFUL,

53
00:02:40,732 --> 00:02:43,001
AND AFTER AWHILE, IT JUST
KINDA BOGGLES YOUR BRAIN.

54
00:02:43,001 --> 00:02:45,036
I TOLD YOU,
GOD GOT PLANS FOR ME.

55
00:02:45,036 --> 00:02:47,138
HE SURE DOES.

56
00:02:47,138 --> 00:02:48,473
TYRA MAIL.

57
00:02:48,473 --> 00:02:51,276
YOU GUYS, COME IN HERE
SO WE CAN READ THE MAIL.

58
00:02:51,276 --> 00:02:55,113
"FIND OUT THE PECKING ORDER
AT 7:00 A.M.-- TYRA."

59
00:02:55,113 --> 00:02:56,381
WHAT IS PECKING ORDER?

60
00:02:56,381 --> 00:02:59,284
THAT'S LIKE
EXCELLENT, GOOD, FAIR, BETTER.

61
00:02:59,284 --> 00:03:00,685
BAD, WORSE.

62
00:03:00,685 --> 00:03:02,254
I'M NOT SURE I LOVE THAT.

63
00:03:08,526 --> 00:03:10,195
HI, GUYS, MY NAME IS JASON.

64
00:03:10,195 --> 00:03:11,663
I'M A FASHION STYLIST,
AND I TEACH AT

65
00:03:11,663 --> 00:03:13,465
THE LONDON COLLEGE OF FASHION.

66
00:03:13,465 --> 00:03:16,234
TODAY, WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO
IS TEACH YOU ALL ABOUT POSING.

67
00:03:16,234 --> 00:03:18,036
WE'RE GONNA GO AROUND LONDON
TODAY AND HAVE

68
00:03:18,036 --> 00:03:19,404
A LOOK AT THE SCULPTURES.

69
00:03:19,404 --> 00:03:22,007
WHAT YOU'VE GOTTA REMEMBER
IS WHEN THESE GUYS ARE POSING

70
00:03:22,007 --> 00:03:24,609
FOR THE SCULPTURE, THEY HAVE
TO STAY IN POSITIONS

71
00:03:24,609 --> 00:03:27,178
AND HOLD POSITIONS
FOR A VERY LONG TIME.

72
00:03:27,178 --> 00:03:29,014
AS A TOP MODEL,
IT'S REALLY IMPORTANT AS WELL

73
00:03:29,014 --> 00:03:30,715
FOR YOU TO BE
ABLE TO CONCENTRATE

74
00:03:30,715 --> 00:03:33,451
ON THE PHOTOGRAPHER
DURING THE SHOOT.

75
00:03:33,451 --> 00:03:35,587
LET'S HEAD OFF TO THE BUS
AND HAVE A DRIVE AROUND LONDON

76
00:03:35,587 --> 00:03:36,955
AND CHECK IT ALL OUT.

77
00:03:40,125 --> 00:03:42,327
THAT IS EROS,
THE GOD OF LOVE.

78
00:03:42,327 --> 00:03:43,595
IT'S GORGEOUS.

79
00:03:43,595 --> 00:03:45,497
IT'S LIKE ONE LONG CURVE
RIGHT DOWN

80
00:03:45,497 --> 00:03:46,698
TO THE END OF THE FOOT.

81
00:03:46,698 --> 00:03:48,566
COULD YOU IMAGINE IF YOU GUYS
HAD TO POSE FOR THAT,

82
00:03:48,566 --> 00:03:50,201
HOW LONG IT WOULD--
HOW LONG DO YOU RECKON

83
00:03:50,201 --> 00:03:52,404
YOU COULD STAND TIPTOEING
WITHOUT MOVING?

84
00:03:56,274 --> 00:03:58,143
I NEVER THOUGHT BEFORE
TO LOOK AT A STATUE AND GO,

85
00:03:58,143 --> 00:04:00,045
"WHY IS IT LIKE THAT?"

86
00:04:00,045 --> 00:04:02,147
IT'S ALL BECAUSE
OF HOW THEY'RE POSED.

87
00:04:02,147 --> 00:04:04,082
IF YOU FALL OUT OF YOUR POSE
JUST THE TINIEST BIT,

88
00:04:04,082 --> 00:04:06,518
THEN YOU CAN
COMPLETELY RUIN SOMETHING.

89
00:04:06,518 --> 00:04:08,720
OKAY, LET'S GET OUT
AND HAVE A LOOK AROUND

90
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:10,622
AND SEE WHAT WE CAN FIND, OKAY?

91
00:04:13,191 --> 00:04:16,227
WE'RE WALKING IN REGENT PARK,
AND WE RUN INTO

92
00:04:16,227 --> 00:04:19,698
THIS BEAUTIFUL STATUE,
AND IT'S MISS J. STANDING UP

93
00:04:19,698 --> 00:04:21,499
IN FULL-ON FREEZE MODE.

94
00:04:21,499 --> 00:04:24,235
HEY, J. VERY GOOD.

95
00:04:24,235 --> 00:04:26,037
SEE HOW FOCUSED HE IS?

96
00:04:26,037 --> 00:04:29,207
HE'S NOT FAZED
BY MY TALKING ABOUT HIM.

97
00:04:29,207 --> 00:04:30,575
I'M SURE HIS EYES
AREN'T EVEN COMING DOWN.

98
00:04:30,575 --> 00:04:33,578
WELL, FOR TODAY'S CHALLENGE
YOU WILL BE JUDGED

99
00:04:33,578 --> 00:04:38,149
ON STATUESQUE POSES,
FOCUS, AND CONCENTRATION.

100
00:04:38,149 --> 00:04:39,951
SO, GIRLS, YOU'RE GONNA
HAVE TO DEAL WITH

101
00:04:39,951 --> 00:04:41,286
ALL THE DISTRACTIONS AROUND YOU.

102
00:04:41,286 --> 00:04:43,455
WHOEVER KEEPS THEIR POSE
THE BEST IS GONNA WIN.

103
00:04:43,455 --> 00:04:45,523
I WILL CHOOSE ONE WINNER,
AND THE WINNER IS GONNA GET

104
00:04:45,523 --> 00:04:47,392
A HUGE SHOPPING SPREE.

105
00:04:47,392 --> 00:04:49,194
QUITE SIMPLE.

106
00:04:49,194 --> 00:04:53,498
SINCE WE'RE GONNA HAVE YOU
POSE LIKE STATUES...

107
00:04:53,498 --> 00:04:55,400
WE'RE GONNA HAVE YOU
LOOK LIKE STATUTES.

108
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,002
WHAT?

109
00:04:59,104 --> 00:05:00,739
THE WARDROBE
FOR THIS CHALLENGE

110
00:05:00,739 --> 00:05:04,242
IS FULL ON BODY PAINT
SO WE COULD LOOK LIKE STATUTES.

111
00:05:04,242 --> 00:05:05,977
I FEEL ABSOLUTELY RIDICULOUS.

112
00:05:09,481 --> 00:05:12,250
WHAT I WOULD LIKE YOU TO DO
IS TO GET UP ON THE PEDESTAL.

113
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:14,285
I GONNA PRESENT YOU
WITH THESE TWO SILVER TRAYS.

114
00:05:14,285 --> 00:05:17,322
I WANT YOU TO CHOOSE
YOUR FIERCEST, STRONGEST POSE

115
00:05:17,322 --> 00:05:18,556
YOU CAN GIVE ME.

116
00:05:18,556 --> 00:05:19,524
COME UP
WITH YOUR POSE.

117
00:05:19,524 --> 00:05:21,559
CHOOSE YOUR FIRST POSE.

118
00:05:21,559 --> 00:05:22,994
YOU READY
FOR YOUR FIRST POSE?

119
00:05:22,994 --> 00:05:23,995
I'M GONNA TIME YOU FOR
A MINUTE, OKAY?

120
00:05:23,995 --> 00:05:26,598
WE'RE COMPETING
FOR A SHOPPING SPREE.

121
00:05:26,598 --> 00:05:28,033
BALANCE IT. YOU READY?

122
00:05:28,033 --> 00:05:29,300
I REALLY WANT TO WIN
THE CHALLENGE

123
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,036
BECAUSE THAT'S PROBABLY
THE COOLEST PRIZE THAT WE'VE

124
00:05:31,036 --> 00:05:32,337
GOTTEN IN A CHALLENGE YET.

125
00:05:32,337 --> 00:05:33,605
GIVE IT A POSE.

126
00:05:33,605 --> 00:05:36,241
I GET UP THERE,
AND I'M THINKING LIKE, OKAY,

127
00:05:36,241 --> 00:05:39,611
I CAN SO DO THIS, AND THIS IS
GONNA BE MY CHALLENGE.

128
00:05:39,611 --> 00:05:42,714
AAH! AAH!

129
00:05:42,714 --> 00:05:45,550
FOCUS, FOCUS.

130
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,485
(coos)

131
00:05:52,157 --> 00:05:53,958
FOCUS, FOCUS.

132
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,296
PIGEONS ARE
THE DIRTIEST BIRDS

133
00:05:58,296 --> 00:05:59,697
YOU COULD POSSIBLY FIND.

134
00:05:59,697 --> 00:06:01,032
I HAVE A PIGEON
ON MY HEAD.

135
00:06:01,032 --> 00:06:02,167
YES, YOU DO, BABY.

136
00:06:02,167 --> 00:06:04,169
BUT THEY ALL ARE TOILET-TRAINED,
DON'T WORRY.

137
00:06:04,169 --> 00:06:05,503
OHH! OHH!

138
00:06:05,503 --> 00:06:07,172
PIGEONS ARE FLYING RATS.

139
00:06:07,172 --> 00:06:08,273
THEY EAT RATS.

140
00:06:08,273 --> 00:06:12,243
THEY'D PROBABLY EAT ME
IF THEY COULD.

141
00:06:12,243 --> 00:06:14,179
WHEN BRE REALIZED
THAT THEY WERE PIGEONS,

142
00:06:14,179 --> 00:06:15,580
SHE LOST IT A BIT.

143
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:16,581
EE!

144
00:06:16,581 --> 00:06:18,349
(coos)

145
00:06:18,349 --> 00:06:20,351
I KIND OF NEEDED TO STEP UP
MY GAME, SO I PUT IT ALL

146
00:06:20,351 --> 00:06:21,319
OUT OF THE MY HEAD.

147
00:06:21,319 --> 00:06:22,487
FANTASTIC.

148
00:06:22,487 --> 00:06:24,189
NIK-- SHE DIDN'T BLINK.

149
00:06:24,189 --> 00:06:27,292
SHE FROZE HER POSE PROPERLY.

150
00:06:27,292 --> 00:06:30,128
I LOVE
THE DOUBLE-HEADED PIGEON HAT.

151
00:06:30,128 --> 00:06:31,496
IT'S BRILLIANT.

152
00:06:31,496 --> 00:06:33,298
I DIDN'T REALLY MIND
THE PIGEONS BY THE END.

153
00:06:33,298 --> 00:06:36,401
IT FELT KIND OF NICE WHEN
THEY WERE SCRATCHING MY HEAD.

154
00:06:36,401 --> 00:06:38,236
THAT WAY, YOU REALLY HAVE YOU
HAVE NO DISTRACTIONS NOW.

155
00:06:38,236 --> 00:06:39,504
YOU CAN'T SEE A DAMN THING.

156
00:06:39,504 --> 00:06:41,005
KIM LACKED
A BIT OF IMAGINATION

157
00:06:41,005 --> 00:06:44,375
WHEN IT CAME TO THE POSES.

158
00:06:44,375 --> 00:06:47,979
JAYLA-- SHE LOOKED LIKE
SHE WAS CONCENTRATING TOO HARD.

159
00:06:47,979 --> 00:06:50,215
OHH!

160
00:06:50,215 --> 00:06:51,549
I JUST STARTED CRYING.

161
00:06:51,549 --> 00:06:53,284
I MADE A FOOL
OF MYSELF.

162
00:06:53,284 --> 00:06:54,686
BUT, SERIOUSLY,
I JUST DON'T LIKE

163
00:06:54,686 --> 00:06:56,287
HUGE BIRDS ON TOP OF ME.

164
00:06:56,287 --> 00:06:58,056
(coos)

165
00:06:58,056 --> 00:07:00,425
FANTASTIC. ALL POSERS DONE.

166
00:07:03,194 --> 00:07:05,663
THIS HAS TO BE
THE FUNNIEST CHALLENGE EVER.

167
00:07:05,663 --> 00:07:07,732
THAT WAS
LITERALLY HUMILIATING.

168
00:07:07,732 --> 00:07:09,734
I AM HUMILIATED.

169
00:07:09,734 --> 00:07:11,202
NICOLE COMPLAINS
ABOUT EVERYTHING.

170
00:07:11,202 --> 00:07:14,005
SERIOUSLY,
I NEVER WANT TO DO THAT AGAIN

171
00:07:14,005 --> 00:07:15,640
WITH THOSE NASTY THINGS.

172
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,709
HER VOICE
IS SO ANNOYING.

173
00:07:17,709 --> 00:07:19,344
IT'S SO SHARP AND ALARMING.

174
00:07:19,344 --> 00:07:21,179
I WAS IN TEARS--
STREAMING DOWN MY FACE

175
00:07:21,179 --> 00:07:22,680
AND LIKE, "AAH!"

176
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,183
MY HAIR IS ALWAYS AT ENDS
WHEN SHE TALKS,

177
00:07:25,183 --> 00:07:26,684
AND I DON'T FEEL
LIKE IT'S A CONVERSATION.

178
00:07:26,684 --> 00:07:28,987
(screaming)

179
00:07:28,987 --> 00:07:30,688
I WAS SERIOUSLY FREAKING OUT.

180
00:07:30,688 --> 00:07:33,191
THOSE BIRDS WERE LIKE--
WHEW.

181
00:07:38,163 --> 00:07:39,964
TODAY, THE WINNER
OF THIS CHALLENGE

182
00:07:39,964 --> 00:07:42,000
GETS TO GO ON A SHOPPING SPREE.

183
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,203
AND THE SHOPPING SPREE
IS WORTH...

184
00:07:45,203 --> 00:07:49,040
$15,000.

185
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,241
OH, MY GOODNESS.

186
00:07:50,241 --> 00:07:52,177
CHILD.

187
00:07:52,177 --> 00:07:54,145
AND NOT ONLY THAT, SHE GETS
TO TAKE TWO FRIENDS

188
00:07:54,145 --> 00:07:55,380
ALONG WITH HER.

189
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:56,548
OH, MY GOODNESS.

190
00:07:56,548 --> 00:07:58,149
I AM GOING TO GO FOR...

191
00:07:58,149 --> 00:08:01,419
OHH!

192
00:08:01,419 --> 00:08:03,188
OKAY. NIK.

193
00:08:03,188 --> 00:08:06,591
YEAH!

194
00:08:06,591 --> 00:08:08,026
THANK YOU.

195
00:08:08,026 --> 00:08:09,160
OH, IT'S BEEN A PLEASURE.

196
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,728
I'VE NEVER WON ANYTHING
HERE BEFORE.

197
00:08:10,728 --> 00:08:12,530
I'VE KIND OF BEEN LIKE
THE GIRL ON THE BOTTOM

198
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:13,698
WHEN IT COMES TO CHALLENGES.

199
00:08:13,698 --> 00:08:15,500
SO IT KIND OF FEELS GOOD
TO BE THE ONE TOP RIGHT NOW.

200
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,101
SO WHO ARE YOU GONNA TAKE?

201
00:08:17,101 --> 00:08:21,539
I'M GONNA TAKE BRE
AND... JAYLA.

202
00:08:21,539 --> 00:08:23,274
ALL THE GOLD GODDESSES.

203
00:08:23,274 --> 00:08:26,110
OH, IT MUST BE
TOUGH.

204
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:30,381
SO YOU'RE GONNA SHOP
TILL YOU DROP, BABY.

205
00:08:30,381 --> 00:08:31,583
THANK YOU.

206
00:08:34,152 --> 00:08:36,254
NICOLE, IF YOU LEAVE
THIS SWEATER ONE MORE TIME,

207
00:08:36,254 --> 00:08:39,090
I PROMISE, I'M GONNA
THROW IT IN THE GARBAGE.

208
00:08:39,090 --> 00:08:41,125
ALL DAY, NICOLE WAS
GETTING ON MY NERVES.

209
00:08:41,125 --> 00:08:44,062
I'M NOT REALLY FEELING
WELL TODAY.

210
00:08:44,062 --> 00:08:47,599
I'M A LITTLE STRESSED.
I WANT GO TO SLEEP.

211
00:08:47,599 --> 00:08:49,133
YOU WANT TO WORK OUT MAYBE?

212
00:08:49,133 --> 00:08:51,035
WORKING OUT
IS SO OVERRATED.

213
00:08:51,035 --> 00:08:52,737
NICOLE IS VERY LOUD
ALL THE TIME,

214
00:08:52,737 --> 00:08:54,606
AND I THINK SHE'S
VERY INCONSIDERATE.

215
00:08:54,606 --> 00:08:56,274
OH, THESE BEDS ARE
SO MUCH MORE BOUNCY

216
00:08:56,274 --> 00:08:57,709
THAN THE ONES AT HOME.

217
00:08:57,709 --> 00:08:59,210
"AT HOME." OH, MY GOD!

218
00:08:59,210 --> 00:09:00,645
I JUST CALLED
THAT HELL HOUSE OUR HOME.

219
00:09:00,645 --> 00:09:03,214
YEAH, I TAKE THAT ONE BACK.

220
00:09:03,214 --> 00:09:05,717
I'M ALREADY AGGRAVATED,
AND SHE JUST BUILDS

221
00:09:05,717 --> 00:09:07,986
AND ADDS TO THAT FRUSTRATION.

222
00:09:07,986 --> 00:09:11,089
(clicking tongue)

223
00:09:11,089 --> 00:09:12,624
I KNOW SHE THINKS I'M LOUD
AND OBNOXIOUS.

224
00:09:12,624 --> 00:09:14,025
I DON'T CARE.

225
00:09:14,025 --> 00:09:15,693
JUST BECAUSE
YOU'RE HAVING A BAD DAY

226
00:09:15,693 --> 00:09:17,562
AND YOU'RE GRUMPY AN ANGRY
ALL OF THE TIME,

227
00:09:17,562 --> 00:09:19,397
DOESN'T MEAN THAT I HAVE
TO STOOP DOWN TO YOUR LEVEL.

228
00:09:19,397 --> 00:09:21,666
LIKE I'M STILL GONNA
HAVE FUN AND BE HAPPY.

229
00:09:23,034 --> 00:09:25,403
GUYS, THERE'S A TYRA MAIL.

230
00:09:25,403 --> 00:09:28,039
YOU, UP.
BRE, UP.

231
00:09:30,275 --> 00:09:32,377
"HAVE YOU EVER FELT LIKE
YOU WERE BEING FRAMED?

232
00:09:32,377 --> 00:09:34,078
TYRA."

233
00:09:34,078 --> 00:09:36,347
I'M EXHAUSTED AND IT'S LIKE
1:00 IN THE MORNING.

234
00:09:36,347 --> 00:09:38,182
I DON'T EVEN SPEND TIME TRYING
TO FIGURE OUT WHAT THE DAY'S

235
00:09:38,182 --> 00:09:39,350
GONNA BE LIKE THE NEXT DAY.

236
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:40,551
I JUST GO TO SLEEP.

237
00:09:43,221 --> 00:09:46,324
SO WE MAKE A GROCERY LIST
AND EVERYBODY GETS SOMETHING

238
00:09:46,324 --> 00:09:47,725
FROM THE STORE.

239
00:09:47,725 --> 00:09:50,328
BUT THEN
I LOOK AT MY GROCERY LIST.

240
00:09:50,328 --> 00:09:52,196
LOOK AT MY RECEIPT,
CHECK TO SEE

241
00:09:52,196 --> 00:09:53,564
IF I GOT EVERYTHING I NEEDED.

242
00:09:53,564 --> 00:09:56,367
WHY IS MY CEREAL BAR BOX
ALREADY OPENED?

243
00:09:56,367 --> 00:09:58,369
HEY, THAT WAS NICE.

244
00:09:58,369 --> 00:09:59,704
WHO DID THAT?

245
00:09:59,704 --> 00:10:01,506
WHO GOT FIRST DIBS
ON MY STUFF?

246
00:10:08,513 --> 00:10:10,014
AND I'M SO HEATED.

247
00:10:10,014 --> 00:10:13,418
DON'T TOUCH MY FOOD.
DON'T TOUCH MY FOOD.

248
00:10:18,189 --> 00:10:20,325
THE PRESSURE IS RIDICULOUS
AT THIS POINT,

249
00:10:20,325 --> 00:10:22,260
AND BRE'S FOOD OBVIOUSLY
IS IMPORTANT TO HER.

250
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:24,562
I MEAN, WHEN PEOPLE START
MESSING WITH, YOU KNOW, FOOD

251
00:10:24,562 --> 00:10:28,333
AND THINGS LIKE THAT,
IT'S GONNA GET REALLY UGLY.

252
00:10:28,333 --> 00:10:31,336
I POURED OUT ALL OF NICOLE'S
CANNED SODAS.

253
00:10:31,336 --> 00:10:33,438
I'VE BEEN DISRESPECTED,
BUT THIS WAS JUST TOO MUCH.

254
00:10:45,416 --> 00:10:48,119
(laughing)

255
00:10:50,288 --> 00:10:51,689
OH, GOD.

256
00:10:51,689 --> 00:10:53,991
BRE, IS THAT REALLY NECESSARY?

257
00:11:09,173 --> 00:11:10,274
GO.

258
00:11:10,274 --> 00:11:13,111
YOU'RE SO SKETCHY.

259
00:11:13,111 --> 00:11:14,245
BRE IS LIKE,
"YOU GO BACK TO YOUR ROOM,

260
00:11:14,245 --> 00:11:16,013
AND YOU GO TO SLEEP NOW
AND DON'T COME BACK IN HERE."

261
00:11:16,013 --> 00:11:17,348
AND AT THIS POINT, YOU KNOW,
I FEEL STUPID

262
00:11:17,348 --> 00:11:18,750
BECAUSE I'M LIKE GETTING
BULLIED AROUND.

263
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:21,586
I WAS DOING JUST FINE
UNTIL YOU WEASELED

264
00:11:21,586 --> 00:11:23,321
YOUR WAY IN HERE.

265
00:11:23,321 --> 00:11:27,325
BUT YOU-- YOUR MIND WANDERS,
THINKS TOO-- TOO MUCH.

266
00:11:27,325 --> 00:11:28,760
YOU HAVE TO FIND OUT.

267
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,128
OF COURSE I DO.

268
00:11:30,128 --> 00:11:31,396
AND I WAS LIKE,
"TELL ME WHAT IS GOING ON.

269
00:11:31,396 --> 00:11:32,764
LIKE TELL ME WHAT YOU TOOK."

270
00:11:32,764 --> 00:11:34,465
AND SHE'S LIKE,
"I DIDN'T DO ANYTHING.

271
00:11:34,465 --> 00:11:36,667
I PUT JAYLA'S DIRTY SOCKS
UNDER NICOLE'S BED."

272
00:11:36,667 --> 00:11:38,770
AND I WAS LIKE, "WHY?"

273
00:11:38,770 --> 00:11:40,805
YOU'RE GONNA FIND SOMETHING
BETTER IN THE MORNING.

274
00:11:40,805 --> 00:11:42,306
I DON'T REALLY
WANT TO BE IN THE DRAMA.

275
00:11:42,306 --> 00:11:44,208
I FEEL LIKE I JUST KINDA
HAVE TO FOCUS ON MYSELF.

276
00:11:44,208 --> 00:11:45,576
I HAVE ENOUGH THINGS
TO WORRY ABOUT.

277
00:11:45,576 --> 00:11:46,778
GOOD NIGHT.

278
00:11:46,778 --> 00:11:48,045
GOOD NIGHT.

279
00:11:48,045 --> 00:11:49,180
I'M JUST GONNA TRY
AND BE CORDIAL

280
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:50,481
AND GET ALONG WITH BRE
AS BEST I CAN

281
00:11:50,481 --> 00:11:52,383
UNTIL ONE OF US IS ELIMINATED

282
00:11:52,383 --> 00:11:54,485
AND THEN I DON'T HAVE TO WORRY
ABOUT HER ANYMORE.

283
00:12:02,393 --> 00:12:05,463
I WON A CHALLENGE,
AND SO THIS MORNING IS THE DAY

284
00:12:05,463 --> 00:12:07,632
WE GET TO GO ON OUR SPREE.

285
00:12:07,632 --> 00:12:08,699
GOOD MORNING.

286
00:12:08,699 --> 00:12:10,768
WE WALK DOWNSTAIRS,
AND WE WERE GREETED BY

287
00:12:10,768 --> 00:12:13,471
A HARRODS' ROLLS-ROYCE.

288
00:12:13,471 --> 00:12:16,641
AND YOU DIDN'T EAT
THEM GRANOLA BARS, RIGHT?

289
00:12:16,641 --> 00:12:18,609
OKAY, WHAT IS THIS
ABOUT THE GRANOLA BARS?

290
00:12:18,609 --> 00:12:20,111
I KNEW IT WAS NICOLE.

291
00:12:20,111 --> 00:12:21,579
THERE'S NOBODY ELSE
IN THE HOUSE.

292
00:12:21,579 --> 00:12:22,680
THERE'S NO GHOSTS.

293
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,148
THERE'S NOTHING.

294
00:12:24,148 --> 00:12:26,083
TO MAKE A LONG STORY SHORT,
I SNUCK IN THE ROOM

295
00:12:26,083 --> 00:12:28,085
AND EMPTIED OUT
ALL OF HER RED BULLS THAT

296
00:12:28,085 --> 00:12:30,588
SHE JUST BOUGHT FROM THE STORE
AND LEFT THEM EMPTY.

297
00:12:35,293 --> 00:12:37,295
I DON'T EVEN HAVE THE ENERGY
TO GET MAD.

298
00:12:37,295 --> 00:12:39,230
I JUST DON'T HAVE
THE ENERGY TO EVEN BE AROUND

299
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:40,298
THESE PEOPLE ANYMORE.

300
00:12:40,298 --> 00:12:42,300
I WAKE UP IN THE MORNING
AND I FIND THAT

301
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:44,035
MY ENERGY DRINKS ARE GONE.

302
00:12:44,035 --> 00:12:46,471
TWO OF THEM ARE OPENED
AND EMPTY IN THE BATHROOM.

303
00:12:46,471 --> 00:12:49,173
I JUST WANT THESE PEOPLE
TO LEAVE. GO HOME.

304
00:12:49,173 --> 00:12:52,176
BACK IN L.A., BRE WAS
THROWING INSULTS AT ME

305
00:12:52,176 --> 00:12:54,779
AND BASHING MY CHARACTER
IN THAT LIMO.

306
00:12:54,779 --> 00:12:57,181
YOU HAVE SOMETHING
TO SAY ABOUT EVERYBODY,

307
00:12:57,181 --> 00:12:59,150
AND I KNOW THAT, SWEETHEART.

308
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:00,284
I KNOW.

309
00:13:00,284 --> 00:13:02,553
LIKE I'M SORRY AND LIKE
I JUST DON'T LIKE--

310
00:13:02,553 --> 00:13:04,322
SOMETIMES I JUST DON'T KNOW.

311
00:13:04,322 --> 00:13:07,091
AT THIS POINT, I'M REALLY UPSET
THAT I APOLOGIZED IN THE LIMO.

312
00:13:07,091 --> 00:13:08,693
I'M JUST STUPID AND LIKE
I JUST LIKE SAY THINGS

313
00:13:08,693 --> 00:13:10,361
FOR COMIC EFFECT.

314
00:13:10,361 --> 00:13:13,130
I THINK THAT BRE IS LIKE
PRETTY JEALOUS OF ME,

315
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:15,132
AND I THINK SHE'S JEALOUS
OF KIM BECAUSE KIM'S DOING

316
00:13:15,132 --> 00:13:16,467
REALLY WELL NOW.

317
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:18,536
WE NEED TO CONCENTRATE ON
HAVING A GOOD PHOTO SHOOT.

318
00:13:18,536 --> 00:13:23,541
SO WE'RE NOT THE ONES
WHO GET... BOOTED.

319
00:13:23,541 --> 00:13:27,211
("Spring" from
Vivaldi's "Four Seasons" plays)

320
00:13:30,348 --> 00:13:32,350
HELLO, GIRLS,
AND WELCOME TO HARRODS.

321
00:13:32,350 --> 00:13:34,552
BY APPOINTMENT
IS A V.I.P. SERVICE

322
00:13:34,552 --> 00:13:36,621
FOR THE ULTIMATE SHOPPING
EXPERIENCE.

323
00:13:36,621 --> 00:13:39,457
NIK, AS THE WINNER,
YOU HAVE A $10,000

324
00:13:39,457 --> 00:13:41,659
SHOPPING SPREE,
AND YOUR PERSONAL SHOPPER

325
00:13:41,659 --> 00:13:43,461
TODAY WILL BE RAYMUNDO.

326
00:13:43,461 --> 00:13:47,131
JAYLA AND BRE, YOU HAVE
$5,000 SHOPPING TO DO TOGETHER

327
00:13:47,131 --> 00:13:49,534
WITH YOUR ASSISTANTS
LAURA AND SIMONE.

328
00:13:49,534 --> 00:13:51,435
SO LET'S GET SHOPPING.

329
00:13:53,271 --> 00:13:55,306
IF YOU SEE ANYTHING CUTE,
JUST TELL ME.

330
00:13:55,306 --> 00:13:56,374
OH, DEAR.

331
00:13:56,374 --> 00:13:57,375
IS THAT WHAT YOU LIKE?

332
00:13:57,375 --> 00:13:58,376
YES.

333
00:13:58,376 --> 00:13:59,377
THIS IS NICE.

334
00:13:59,377 --> 00:14:00,378
DON'T LIKE THAT?

335
00:14:00,378 --> 00:14:01,345
NO.

336
00:14:01,345 --> 00:14:02,346
THAT'S SO POLICE, GIRL.

337
00:14:02,346 --> 00:14:03,347
THAT IS GORGEOUS.

338
00:14:03,347 --> 00:14:04,348
THEY'RE NICE.

339
00:14:04,348 --> 00:14:05,349
YEAH.

340
00:14:05,349 --> 00:14:06,617
WHAT ABOUT BAGS?

341
00:14:06,617 --> 00:14:08,252
BAGS?
HOW MUCH IS THAT ONE?

342
00:14:08,252 --> 00:14:09,554
REGULAR PRICE IS $1,400.

343
00:14:09,554 --> 00:14:12,256
IT'S KINDA COOL JUST
TO BE LIKE, "I WANT THIS ONE

344
00:14:12,256 --> 00:14:14,058
AND THIS ONE,
AND I THINK I LIKE THIS ONE."

345
00:14:14,058 --> 00:14:16,260
IT MAKES YOU FEEL LIKE
YOU'VE MADE IT.

346
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:18,062
I DON'T WANNA BE AVERAGE.
I WANT TO BE FIERCE.

347
00:14:18,062 --> 00:14:19,063
I KNOW.

348
00:14:19,063 --> 00:14:20,064
HONEY, YOU'RE SHOPPING WITH ME.

349
00:14:20,064 --> 00:14:21,098
YOU'LL BE FIERCE, TRUST ME.

350
00:14:21,098 --> 00:14:22,266
WANNA HAVE A LOOK
AT MARC JACOBS?

351
00:14:22,266 --> 00:14:23,401
YEAH.

352
00:14:23,401 --> 00:14:24,769
I HATE THIS.

353
00:14:24,769 --> 00:14:26,070
OKAY, I'M THINKING
WE'VE GOT A FEW T-SHIRTS.

354
00:14:26,070 --> 00:14:27,405
WE'VE GOT AT LEAST THREE PAIRS
OF JEANS.

355
00:14:27,405 --> 00:14:28,773
THIS IN A SMALL.

356
00:14:28,773 --> 00:14:31,075
IT IS DEFINITELY RETAIL THERAPY.

357
00:14:31,075 --> 00:14:32,109
ARE WE TAKING THIS ONE?

358
00:14:32,109 --> 00:14:33,444
YEP.

359
00:14:33,444 --> 00:14:34,512
ALL OF THE STRESS THAT WAS
GOING ON TODAY JUST KIND OF

360
00:14:34,512 --> 00:14:37,181
LIFTED OFF OF MY CHEST,
AND I JUST FELT LIKE I WAS IN

361
00:14:37,181 --> 00:14:38,583
A DIFFERENT PLACE FOR ONCE.

362
00:14:38,583 --> 00:14:39,717
NIK, DID YOU SEE
YOUR HANDBAG?

363
00:14:39,717 --> 00:14:41,085
YES, I DID.

364
00:14:41,085 --> 00:14:42,720
MY FAVORITE THING I GOT
WAS THIS PURSE.

365
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:44,422
I DON'T EVEN KNOW THE BRAND.

366
00:14:44,422 --> 00:14:46,290
I JUST KNOW IT COSTS
A WHOLE LOT OF MONEY.

367
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:48,359
HONEY, I THINK WE'VE ACTUALLY
DONE REALLY WELL.

368
00:14:48,359 --> 00:14:49,760
WE GOT BETTER STUFF
THAN EVERYBODY ELSE.

369
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:51,228
BUT SINCE WE HAVE TIME...

370
00:14:51,228 --> 00:14:53,331
OH, WE HAVE TIME.
WE'RE GONNA GET MORE STUFF.

371
00:15:02,807 --> 00:15:05,409
SO AFTER THE SHOPPING SPREE,
WE WENT TO OUR PHOTO SHOOT

372
00:15:05,409 --> 00:15:10,181
WHERE KIM AND NICOLE
ARE WAITING FOR US.

373
00:15:10,181 --> 00:15:11,582
HEY.

374
00:15:11,582 --> 00:15:13,184
HIS BOOBS LOOK FABULOUS.

375
00:15:13,184 --> 00:15:14,518
MY BOOBS LOOK
FABULOUS?

376
00:15:14,518 --> 00:15:15,753
YEAH, I KNOW, THEY'RE GREAT.

377
00:15:15,753 --> 00:15:17,455
THERE'S A REASON I'M WEARING
THIS LITTLE CRAZY TOP,

378
00:15:17,455 --> 00:15:19,256
BUT I'M GONNA TELL YOU
ABOUT THAT IN A SECOND.

379
00:15:19,256 --> 00:15:21,459
TODAY YOU GIRLS ARE ACTUALLY
DOING A PHOTO SHOOT

380
00:15:21,459 --> 00:15:25,162
FOR OLAY QUENCH,
A NEW BODY LOTION FROM OLAY.

381
00:15:25,162 --> 00:15:27,264
NOW BACK IN THE DAY,
MODELS USED TO SIT

382
00:15:27,264 --> 00:15:30,167
FOR HOURS AND HOURS FOR ARTISTS
AS THEY PAINTED

383
00:15:30,167 --> 00:15:31,769
AND SCULPTED THEM.

384
00:15:31,769 --> 00:15:35,139
NOW, YOU GIRLS ARE GONNA HAVE
TO USE THAT SAME CONCENTRATION

385
00:15:35,139 --> 00:15:39,176
TODAY AS WE RE-CREATE CLASSIC
ART WITH A MODERN TWIST.

386
00:15:39,176 --> 00:15:41,245
NOW BEHIND ME, THE SETUP
THAT'S GOING UP

387
00:15:41,245 --> 00:15:43,347
IS "THE BIRTH OF VENUS."

388
00:15:43,347 --> 00:15:45,316
AND, ACTUALLY, KIM, YOU ARE
GONNA BE "THE BIRTH OF VENUS."

389
00:15:45,316 --> 00:15:46,617
DO YOU KNOW THAT PIECE OF ART,
BY THE WAY?

390
00:15:46,617 --> 00:15:48,119
YEAH.

391
00:15:48,119 --> 00:15:49,320
NICOLE, ARE YOU FAMILIAR WITH

392
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,621
THE
"GIRL WITH THE PEARL EARRING"?

393
00:15:50,621 --> 00:15:52,289
SO THAT'S GONNA BE YOU.

394
00:15:52,289 --> 00:15:53,758
ALL RIGHT, NIK, YOUR CHALLENGE--
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO BE

395
00:15:53,758 --> 00:15:55,726
THE "VITRUVIAN MAN,"
WHICH IS STRAIGHT ON,

396
00:15:55,726 --> 00:15:57,495
ARMS OUT, LEGS OUT.

397
00:15:57,495 --> 00:16:00,631
SO YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
TO CONFRONT THAT FACE ON POSE.

398
00:16:00,631 --> 00:16:03,300
BRE, YOU'VE GOT THAT LITTLE
SUBTLE SOMETHING GOING ON

399
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:04,402
GOING UNDERNEATH THERE.

400
00:16:04,402 --> 00:16:07,738
YOU ARE GOING TO BE
THE "MONA LISA," ALL RIGHT?

401
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:09,674
JAYLA, DO YOU KNOW WHO
"WHISTLER'S MOTHER" IS?

402
00:16:09,674 --> 00:16:11,075
YEP.

403
00:16:11,075 --> 00:16:12,309
IT'S ALL
ABOUT PROFILE AND NECK,

404
00:16:12,309 --> 00:16:13,811
AND YOU AND I HAVE TALKED
ABOUT NECK SO MUCH,

405
00:16:13,811 --> 00:16:15,279
SO THAT'S WHAT
YOU'RE DOING TODAY.

406
00:16:15,279 --> 00:16:16,414
SO DON'T YOU GET THIS?

407
00:16:16,414 --> 00:16:18,482
THIS IS MY MODERN INTERPRETATION
OF MY CLASSIC ART.

408
00:16:18,482 --> 00:16:20,084
FEEL IT?
ALL RIGHT.

409
00:16:20,084 --> 00:16:23,287
I'M EXCITED, AND YOU GUYS
SHOULD BE SUPER EXCITED BECAUSE

410
00:16:23,287 --> 00:16:26,123
I'VE GOT A VERY SPECIAL GUEST
WHO'S GONNA INTRODUCE

411
00:16:26,123 --> 00:16:28,726
AN EXTRA, EXTRA SPECIAL GUEST.

412
00:16:28,726 --> 00:16:31,062
TWIGGY, COME ON OUT HERE.

413
00:16:31,062 --> 00:16:34,732
THIS IS THE MAN
WHO CHANGED MY LIFE.

414
00:16:34,732 --> 00:16:38,569
HE TOOK MY FIRST PHOTOGRAPH
IN 1966.

415
00:16:38,569 --> 00:16:40,271
HIS NAME IS BARRY LATEGAN.

416
00:16:40,271 --> 00:16:41,772
AS YOU KNOW, I'VE TALKED
ABOUT HIM ALL THROUGH THE SHOW.

417
00:16:41,772 --> 00:16:44,542
THE GUY WHO PHOTOGRAPHED ME
IS A GENIUS.

418
00:16:44,542 --> 00:16:48,245
HE'S A MAN CALLED BARRY LATEGAN,
WHO STILL WORKS IN LONDON.

419
00:16:48,245 --> 00:16:51,582
AND I HAVE TO SAY,
THE HAIRCUT WAS VERY IMPORTANT,

420
00:16:51,582 --> 00:16:54,485
BUT BEING PHOTOGRAPHED
BY SOMEBODY AS BRILLIANT AS YOU,

421
00:16:54,485 --> 00:16:56,654
IT DID CHANGE MY WHOLE CAREER.

422
00:16:56,654 --> 00:17:00,324
YOU ARE ALL GOING TO BE
REPRESENTING IN A MODERN SENSE

423
00:17:00,324 --> 00:17:03,427
THE WAY BEAUTY HAS BEEN
LOOKED AT IN THE PAST.

424
00:17:03,427 --> 00:17:06,063
WE'RE NOT GOING TO LOOK AT YOU
LIKE A ROW OF TOMATOES

425
00:17:06,063 --> 00:17:07,264
WHERE YOU ALL LOOK ALIKE.

426
00:17:07,264 --> 00:17:08,866
YOU GIRLS DON'T EVEN KNOW.

427
00:17:08,866 --> 00:17:10,401
MOST GIRLS DON'T GET
THE OPPORTUNITY

428
00:17:10,401 --> 00:17:13,804
TO BE SHOT BY A WORLD-RENOWNED
PHOTOGRAPHER SUCH AS BARRY.

429
00:17:18,541 --> 00:17:20,544
THE FIRST PERSON THAT
APPROACHES ME IS KIM.

430
00:17:20,544 --> 00:17:25,149
SHE'S LIKE, "TELL ME YOU'RE
GONNA PAY FOR NICOLE'S DRINKS."

431
00:17:25,149 --> 00:17:26,550
SHE'S BEEN TALKING ABOUT IT.

432
00:17:26,550 --> 00:17:27,617
I WAS LIKE...

433
00:17:27,617 --> 00:17:29,353
I DON'T WANNA TALK ABOUT IT.

434
00:17:29,353 --> 00:17:30,654
OKAY, BUT WHY ARE YOU
MAD AT ME? I'M JUST SAYING--

435
00:17:30,654 --> 00:17:32,323
I'M NOT MAD AT YOU.

436
00:17:32,323 --> 00:17:33,758
I WAS LIKE,
"WHAT?

437
00:17:33,758 --> 00:17:36,127
HELLO, HI."

438
00:17:36,127 --> 00:17:37,428
I THINK YOU SHOULD MIND
YOUR BUSINESS.

439
00:17:37,428 --> 00:17:39,263
I DON'T WANNA GET INTO IT.

440
00:17:39,263 --> 00:17:41,766
ALL RIGHT, I JUST--
YOU KNOW... I DON'T KNOW.

441
00:17:41,766 --> 00:17:44,101
IT'S JUST OTHER PEOPLE'S STUFF.

442
00:17:44,101 --> 00:17:46,771
IT SUCKS WHEN PEOPLE
TOUCH YOUR STUFF, RIGHT?

443
00:17:46,771 --> 00:17:48,305
YEAH, I MEAN, I GUESS SO.

444
00:17:48,305 --> 00:17:49,607
YEAH, I THINK SO, TOO.

445
00:17:49,607 --> 00:17:51,442
YEAH, THAT'S WHY I WANNA SAY
Y'ALL COULD JUST REPLACE IT

446
00:17:51,442 --> 00:17:52,610
SO WE DON'T HAVE TO DEAL
WITH IT, YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

447
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:53,744
NO.

448
00:17:53,744 --> 00:17:55,279
OKAY, THEN FINE, THEN DON'T.

449
00:17:55,279 --> 00:17:57,314
KIM WAS TRYING TO MEDIATE,
BUT SHE GOT HERSELF

450
00:17:57,314 --> 00:17:59,316
STUCK IN THE MIDDLE OF IT,
SO SHE KIND OF DREW HERSELF

451
00:17:59,316 --> 00:18:02,153
INTO THE PROBLEM
THAT SHE WAS TRYING TO FIX.

452
00:18:02,153 --> 00:18:03,654
SERIOUSLY, KIM, I FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE PLAYING

453
00:18:03,654 --> 00:18:05,022
BOTH SIDES OF THE FENCE.

454
00:18:05,022 --> 00:18:06,457
I'M PLAYING NO SIDES
OF THE FENCE.

455
00:18:06,457 --> 00:18:08,492
YOU DON'T TRUST ME,
AND YOU CAN TRUST ME.

456
00:18:08,492 --> 00:18:10,161
AAH!

457
00:18:10,161 --> 00:18:11,595
I JUST NEED A CORNER.

458
00:18:11,595 --> 00:18:12,763
